-i\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Sun Shih-i\">Sun Shih-i</a></div><div class=\"wst-header-forward-arrow\">\u2192</div></div></div><div class=\"wst-header-notes header&#95;notes searchaux wst-unknown-notes\"><style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r14791120\">.mw-parser-output .plainSister{display:block;font-size:93%;line-height:normal;list-style-type:none;list-style-image:none;list-style-position:outside;border:1px solid var(--border-color-interactive--hover,#AAA);float:right;clear:right;margin:0.5ex 0 0.5ex 0.5ex;padding:0;background:var(--background-color-base,#FFFFFF);color:var(--color-base,#202122)}.mw-parser-output .sisicon,.mw-parser-output .dabicon{padding-right:1ex}</style><ul class=\"plainSister\"><li class=\"sisitem\"><span class=\"sisicon\"><span typeof=\"mw:File/Frameless\"><a href=\"/wiki/Special:SiteMatrix\" title=\"Special:SiteMatrix\"><img alt=\"Sister Projects\" src=\"//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Wikimedia-logo.svg/20px-Wikimedia-logo.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikisource.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Wikimedia-logo.svg/40px-Wikimedia-logo.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikisource.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"1024\" data-file-height=\"1024\" /></a></span></span><a href=\"/wiki/Special:SiteMatrix\" title=\"Special:SiteMatrix\">sister projects</a>: <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q107367702\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"d:Q107367702\">Wikidata item</a></li></ul></div><div class=\"ws-noexport\" id=\"ws-data\" style=\"speak:none\"><span id=\"ws-article-id\">3654401</span><span id=\"ws-title\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period\">Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period</a>, Volume 2 \u2014 Sun Sh\u00ean-hsing</span><span id=\"ws-editor\">Arthur W. Hummel</span><span id=\"ws-author\">George A. Kennedy</span></div></div>\n<p><span style=\"display:none\" id=\"dynamic&#95;layout&#95;overrider\">Layout 2</span>\n</p>\n<div class=\"prp-pages-output\" lang=\"en\">\n<span><span class=\"pagenum ws-pagenum\" id=\"679\" data-page-number=\"679\" data-page-name=\"Page:Eminent Chinese Of The Ch\u2019ing Period - Hummel - 1943 - Vol. 2.pdf/77\" data-page-index=\"77\" data-page-quality=\"3\" title=\"Page:Eminent&#95;Chinese&#95;Of&#95;The&#95;Ch%E2%80%99ing&#95;Period&#95;-&#95;Hummel&#95;-&#95;1943&#95;-&#95;Vol.&#95;2.pdf/77\"><span id=\"pageindex&#95;77\" class=\"pagenum-inner ws-noexport\">&#8203;</span></span></span><b>SUN</b> Sh\u00ean-hsing \u5b6b\u613c\u884c (<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r14767791\">.mw-parser-output .wst-tooltip{cursor:help;border-bottom:thin dotted cornflowerblue}.mw-parser-output .wst-tooltip-nodash{border-bottom:none}</style><span class=\"wst-tooltip wst-tooltip-dash\" title=\"Courtesy name (Tz\u00fb/Zi, \u5b57)\">T.</span>&#160;\u805e\u65af,&#32;<link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r14767791\" /><span class=\"wst-tooltip wst-tooltip-dash\" title=\"Literary name (Hao, \u865f)\">H.</span>&#160;\u6dc7\u6fb3), 1565\u20131636, Feb. 18, Ming official, was a native of Wu-chin, Kiangsu. He ranked third as <i>chin-shih</i> in 1595 and was appointed a Hanlin compiler, but retired a few years later to devote himself to study in strict seclusion. In 1613 he was made junior vice-president and acting head of the Board of Ceremonies, in which capacity he attacked various irregularities that had arisen through twenty years of complete neglect of governmental affairs on the part of Emperor Sh\u00ean-tsung. In the following year he retired\u2014this time until 1621 when he was given the presidency of the same Board. The death of the Ming Emperor Kuang-tsung (see <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Chu_Ch%27ang-lo\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Chu Ch&#39;ang-lo\">Chu Ch'ang-lo</a></span>) had occurred under suspicious circumstances. Taken ill less than ten days after ascending the throne, he rapidly grew worse and died after being given a pill of \"red lead\" by the sub-director of the Court of State Ceremonial. When this official was accused by the censor of criminal negligence he was shielded by the Grand Secretary, Fang Ts'ung-ch\u00ea (see under <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Chu_Ch%27ang-lo\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Chu Ch&#39;ang-lo\">Chu Ch'ang-lo</a></span>). Sun denounced the latter as the murderer of the late emperor and demanded his execution. As a result the official who had administered the pill was exiled, although Fang escaped an investigation. Shortly afterward Sun resigned on account of illness and was kept out of office thereafter by the eunuch, <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Wei_Chung-hsien\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Wei Chung-hsien\">Wei Chung-hsien</a></span>&#32;[<i>q.&#8239;v.</i>]. In 1627 he was condemned to banishment, but the sentence was not carried out owing to the fall of the eunuch party. Though he was often recommended at Court for the post of a Grand Secretary, it was not until 1635 that he was again summoned to take part in the government. Soon after reaching Peking he took ill and died, at the age of seventy-two (<i>sui</i>). He was granted posthumously the title of Senior Guardian of the Heir Apparent, and was canonized as W\u00ean-chieh \u6587\u4ecb.<div class=\"&#95;&#95;nop wst-nop\"></div>\n<p>&#32;<span><span class=\"pagenum ws-pagenum\" id=\"680\" data-page-number=\"680\" data-page-name=\"Page:Eminent Chinese Of The Ch\u2019ing Period - Hummel - 1943 - Vol. 2.pdf/78\" data-page-index=\"78\" data-page-quality=\"3\" title=\"Page:Eminent&#95;Chinese&#95;Of&#95;The&#95;Ch%E2%80%99ing&#95;Period&#95;-&#95;Hummel&#95;-&#95;1943&#95;-&#95;Vol.&#95;2.pdf/78\"><span id=\"pageindex&#95;78\" class=\"pagenum-inner ws-noexport\">&#8203;</span></span></span>Sun Sh\u00ean-hsing was the great-great-grandfather of the eminent scholar, <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Sun_Hsing-yen\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Sun Hsing-yen\">Sun Hsing-yen</a></span>&#32;[<i>q.&#8239;v.</i>].\n</p>\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r15431518\">.mw-parser-output .wst-rule{background-color:currentcolor;color:inherit;width:auto;margin:2px auto 2px auto;height:1px;overflow:hidden}.mw-parser-output .wst-rule.wst-rule-left{margin-left:0}.mw-parser-output .wst-rule.wst-rule-right{margin-right:0}.mw-parser-output .wst-rule.__uirule{background-color:#a2a9b1;color:inherit;border:0;margin-top:0.2em;margin-bottom:0.2em}</style><hr class=\"wst-rule wst-rule-left\" style=\"color:inherit;width:40%;\" />\n<p>[M.1/243/11a; M.39/21/1a; <i>Wu-chin Yang-hu ho-chih</i> (see under <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Li_Chao-lo\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Li Chao-lo\">Li Chao-lo</a></span>) 21/1a.]\n</p>\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r15431519\">.mw-parser-output .wst-right{text-align:right}</style><div class=\"wst-right\" style=\"margin-right:2em;\">\n<p><span class=\"smallcaps\" style=\"font-variant:small-caps;\">George A. Kennedy</span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<p><br />\n&#32;\n</p>\n</div>\n</div>"},"links":[{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Chu Ch'ang-lo"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Li Chao-lo"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Sun Hsing-yen"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Sun K'o-wang"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Sun Shih-i"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Wei Chung-hsien"},{"ns":102,"exists":"","*":"Author:Arthur W. Hummel"},{"ns":102,"exists":"","*":"Author:George A. Kennedy"}],"sections":[],"wikitext":{"*":"{{Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period\n | volume   = 2\n | onlysection = sun shen-hsing\n | previous = Sun K'o-wang\n | next     = Sun Shih-i\n | from     = 77\n | to       = 78\n | notes    =\n | section_author = George A. Kennedy\n}}{{DEFAULTSORT:Sun Sh\u00ean-hsing}}"}}}